WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:18.685
For many nights after the children saved the train, Bobbie woke up screaming with nightmares.

2
00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:22.208
One morning a letter arrived.

3
00:00:23.328 --> 00:00:25.350
It was addressed to Peter, Bobbie, and Phyllis.

4
00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:28.453
Curious, they opened the letter quickly.

5
00:00:29.393 --> 00:00:36.039
It said: Dear Sir and Ladies, Thank you for saving the train and stopping a very bad accident.

6
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.282
Please come to the station at three o'clock, on the 30th of the month.

7
00:00:41.703 --> 00:00:43.345
Yours faithfully, J.

8
00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:51.131
Inglewood Secretary of the Great Northern and Southern Railway Company It was to be a special day indeed.

9
00:00:52.572 --> 00:00:55.815
The children went to the station at three o'clock, dressed in their best clothes.

10
00:00:56.916 --> 00:00:58.537
The stationmaster came to meet them.

11
00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:01.500
"Come into the waiting room," he said.

12
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.681
The waiting room looked very different today.

13
00:01:06.101 --> 00:01:09.142
There was a carpet on the floor and roses on the windowsills.

14
00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:11.683
Green branches hung from the wall.

15
00:01:12.703 --> 00:01:16.644
Perks, the porter, was there, as well as several men with tall hats.

16
00:01:17.764 --> 00:01:19.765
There were ladies in expensive dresses too.

17
00:01:21.685 --> 00:01:24.206
Best of all, the old gentleman from the train was there.

18
00:01:25.206 --> 00:01:27.567
He came across the room to shake the children's hands.

19
00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:30.608
Then an important-looking man stood up.

20
00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:34.117
He spoke about how bravely the children had acted.

21
00:01:35.797 --> 00:01:39.118
Next the old gentleman got up and said nice things about the children too.

22
00:01:40.178 --> 00:01:44.940
Then he called the children one by one, and gave each of them a beautiful gold watch and

23
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.381
chain. Inside the watches there was a message.

24
00:01:53.422 --> 00:01:54.382
You were very brave.

25
00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:57.263
Thank you for stopping a train accident.

26
00:01:58.323 --> 00:01:59.964
From the Directors of the Railway Company.

27
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:07.524
The stationmaster whispered to Bobbie, "Now you must make a speech and thank everyone," and he gently pushed

28
00:02:07.584 --> 00:02:08.204
Bobbie forward.

29
00:02:08.224 --> 00:02:11.826
"Oh dear," said Bobbie.

30
00:02:12.947 --> 00:02:17.070
"Ladies and gentlemen," she began, "thank you for these lovely watches.

31
00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:22.453
We really don't deserve them, because what we did wasn't anything really.

32
00:02:23.293 --> 00:02:27.376
Well, it was exciting and frightening Oh, thank you all very much!"

33
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.222
The people clapped, and then everybody shook hands with the three children.

34
00:02:33.663 --> 00:02:34.723
It was a wonderful day.

35
00:02:35.784 --> 00:02:38.826
Afterward the old gentleman walked with them to their little white house.

36
00:02:38.846 --> 00:02:43.408
"I want to meet the mother of these brave and clever children," he said.

37
00:02:44.929 --> 00:02:46.710
Mother was surprised to see their visitor.

38
00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:51.053
She thanked the old man again for the things he had sent when she was ill.

39
00:02:52.073 --> 00:02:56.436
While they had tea and buns, the children told Mother about the people at the station.

40
00:02:57.756 --> 00:03:00.537
Mother and the old gentleman chatted in French and English.

41
00:03:02.638 --> 00:03:07.180
When it was time for the old gentleman to leave, Mother said, "Lovely to meet you.

42
00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.901
I want to thank you for everything."

43
00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:13.162
Then the children waved good-bye to the old gentleman.

44
00:03:14.223 --> 00:03:17.244
It was just as they did every morning when his train passed by.
